<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Valens</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 378 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century">4th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Valens was Roman emperor in the east from 364 until his death in 378 CE. He allowed Gothic refugees to cross the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a> into the empire, but their mistreatment led to revolt. He was killed at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-adrianople">Battle of Adrianople</a> in 378, along with a large part of the eastern Roman army, a disaster that marked a turning point in the empire's decline.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/valens.jpg" alt="Valens" width="320" height="315" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: АНО &quot;Международный нумизматический клуб&quot; · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:INC-3015-a_%D0%A1%D0%BE%D0%BB%D0%B8%D0%B4._%D0%92%D0%B0%D0%BB%D0%B5%D0%BD%D1%82_II._%D0%9E%D0%BA._364_%D0%B3._(%D0%B0%D0%B2%D0%B5%D1%80%D1%81).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
